keeping on top of your pet's health is  just as important as monitoring your own  cancer is unfortunately common in dogs  and there are a number of different  types of cancer that affect them some  more serious and invasive than others  and all require veterinary attention  the earlier cancer can be detected the  better the chances of successful  treatment that's why it's so important  to bring your dog to the vet for routine  wellness exams and the first signs of  any illness dr j.b ogenstein of oasis  animal hospital in henderson says the  majority of her clients stayed up to  date with their pet exams during the  pandemic  she says it's important to know what's  normal and abnormal on your pet so she  recommends the following make sure  you're touching your pet all over you  know running you're not just petting the  top of the head and down the back but  actually literally running your hands  over the body  under the jaw down the legs into the  armpits  down the back legs into the groin and  just feeling  so you know what's normal on your pets  this should happen a minimum of once a  month but as your pet gets older more  frequently she says as some of the  aggressive tumors can grow fairly  quickly
 

